The provided `LambdaObserver` is a thin delegating wrapper around user‑supplied lambdas and standard RxJava plumbing. Its behavior is primarily I/O‑oriented (callback invocation) and its performance is dominated by the supplied `Consumer`/`Action` implementations rather than any intrinsic algorithmic work. Consequently, a microbenchmark would not yield meaningful, isolated performance data, and typical usage should be measured in the context of a full reactive stream rather than this class alone. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.